    {
      "field": "blocks[1].text",
      "before": "A good compost bin should have a waterproof lid, sturdy sides, a rodent-resistant base and an opening you can actually empty through. Bigger bins are best; they retain heat and moisture better.",
      "after": "A good compost bin should have a waterproof lid, sturdy sides, a rodent-resistant base and an opening you can actually empty through. Bigger bins are best; they retain heat and moisture better. You can buy PVC starter bins but beware of poorly fitting lids and front hatches - best is to make your own (see below)."
    },
    {
      "field": "makeYourOwn.text",
      "before": "You can make your own compost bins with brick or timber sides and wooden lids.",
      "after": "A purpose-built compost bin is best. You can recycle old materials such as pallets, or buy and build from new. Edges should fit together tightly to exclude rodents. Sides should penetrate the soil for the same reason."
    }
  ],
